{"records":[{"id":"7x237xf2m3","title":"Computational framework identifies contributing factors for differences between PANoptosis clusters in multiple cancer types","description":"The importance of inflammatory cell death in cancer is increasingly being recognized as this type of death can promote or stall tumorigenesis depending on the cellular context. A unique form of inflammatory cell death, PANoptosis, has been shown to play a role in cancer proliferation in murine models. Further, a recent computational study has shown that, through pancancer transcriptomic profiling of genes involved in PANoptosis, patients can be stratified into PANoptosis High and PANoptosis Low cluster and this classification has significant differences in prognostic associations (overall survival) for low grade gliomas (LGG), kidney and renal cell carcinoma (KIRC) and skin cutaneous melanoma (SKCM) cancers . Here, we perform a comprehensive comparison of molecular characteristics including genetic, genomic, tumor microenvironment composition and immune activation, and pathway enrichments between PANoptosis High and PANoptosis Low clusters to determine their relevance in driving the differential prognostic associations for LGG, KIRC and SKCM cancers.  By identifying various biological features, we can drive better prognostic implications for at risk stratified patient populations based on the PANoptosis phenotype in LGG, KIRC and SKCM cancers. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-10T15:49:26.882Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7x237xf2m3","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7x237xf2m3"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Raghvendra","last_name":"Mall","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thirumala-Devi","last_name":"Kanneganti","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Immunology","Cancer","Cell Death","Computational Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2648w95g9x","title":"Comparison of s-1 plus oxaliplatin (SOX) and capecitabine plus oxaliplatin (CAPOX) as adjuvant chemotherapies in patients with advanced gastric cancer after laparoscopic D2 gastrectomy: a randomized, controlled clinical trial","description":"This data is for \"Comparison of s-1 plus oxaliplatin (SOX) and capecitabine plus oxaliplatin (CAPOX) as adjuvant chemotherapies in patients with advanced gastric cancer after laparoscopic D2 gastrectomy: a randomized, controlled clinical trial\".","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-02-13T14:56:39.601Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2648w95g9x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2648w95g9x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Liu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Surgery","Chemotherapy"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"5drb9c5y9h","title":"Pancancer Transcriptomic Profiling Identifies Key PANoptosis Markers as Therapeutic Targets","description":"Data downloaded from TCGA to perform tumor stratification into PANoptosis clusters based on a PANoptosis gene signature. We design a systematic framework to determine the key innate immune biomarkers for cancers where PANoptosis has a prognostic association with overall survival. More details about the results from the framework are provided in the README. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-12T14:23:47.514Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/5drb9c5y9h","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/5drb9c5y9h"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Raghvendra","last_name":"Mall","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ratnakar","last_name":"Bynigeri","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Rajendra","last_name":"Karki","orcid":null},{"first_name":"RKSUBBARAO","last_name":"MALIREDDI","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Thirumala-Devi","last_name":"Kanneganti","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bhesh","last_name":"Sharma","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Machine Learning","RNA Sequencing","Transcriptomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"w9s35sk673","title":"1H-NMR based metabolomics technology identifies potential serum biomarkers of colorectal cancer lung metastasis in a mouse model","description":"Lung metastasis is a common site of metastasis that reduces the quality of life and survival rates of colorectal cancer patients. The identification of potential diagnostic biomarkers is of great significance to treating lung metastasis in colorectal cancer. In the present study, the metabonomic profiling of serum samples of lung metastasis mice was carried out by using 1H-nuclear magnetic resonance (1H-NMR). The changes in metabolic phenotypes during the progression of lung metastasis of colorectal cancer were noticeable, and some metabolites were identified.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-10-27T12:58:27.03Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/w9s35sk673","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/w9s35sk673"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yan","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Metastasis","Metabolite","Colorectal Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vknp983sbf","title":"Data to accompany Cancer stem cell marker phenotypization and methylation status detection in Slovak colorectal cancer patients","description":"Data accompanying 'Cancer stem cell marker phenotypization and methylation status detection in Slovak colorectal cancer patients' by Mersakova et al.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-02-09T15:30:05.985Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vknp983sbf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vknp983sbf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Sandra","last_name":"Mersakova","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Stem Cell","Methylation","Colorectal Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"bjdg7rynd8","title":"Cadiac function of colorectal cancer mice is remotely controlled by gut microbiota: regulating serum metabolites and myocardial cytokines. Zhan-Kui Gao et al.","description":"In this study, we identified cardiac dysfunction in azomethane and dextran sodium sulfate-induced colorectal cancer mice. Intestinal microbes from healthy mice were transferred to colorectal cancer mice, which vastly reversed the disorder of the gut microbiota and effectively alleviated cardiac dysfunction. Moreover, FMT regulated the expression of serum metabolites such as andrographolide, UTP, and tiamulin, as well as cytokines like TGF-β, IRF5, and β-MHC in the heart. These findings uncover that the disturbed gut microbiota causes cardiac dysfunction in colorectal cancer mice by modulating the expression of serum metabolites and cytokines, which could be alleviated by treatment with FMT.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-07-01T18:01:27.843Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/bjdg7rynd8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/bjdg7rynd8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"占魁","last_name":"高","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chao-Yuan","last_name":"Fan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bo-Wen","last_name":"Zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jia-Xin","last_name":"Geng","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xing","last_name":"Han","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Dan-Qi","last_name":"Xu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Muhammad","last_name":"Arshad","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Hao-Xuan","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jiong-Yi","last_name":"Li","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiao-Qin","last_name":"Mu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cardiovascular Disease","Colorectal Cancer","Intestinal Microbiota"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mv5zpks7mt","title":"Included study probiotic Nisin","description":"This study aims to systematically evaluate the therapeutic potential of nisin-based interventions in colorectal cancer through a comprehensive review of in vivo studies. Nisin, a naturally occurring antimicrobial peptide produced by Lactococcus lactis, has attracted increasing research interest due to its potential anticancer properties, including the modulation of cancer cell proliferation, induction of apoptosis, and regulation of tumor-related biological pathways. This systematic review examines preclinical evidence from animal models to identify the therapeutic effects, underlying mechanisms of action, treatment outcomes, and potential safety profiles of nisin-based interventions in colorectal cancer. A systematic literature search is conducted using major scientific databases, including PubMed, Scopus, and ScienceDirect, following the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses (PRISMA) guidelines. The included studies are critically evaluated to assess methodological quality, risk of bias, and the consistency of reported findings. The review is expected to provide a comprehensive understanding of the current preclinical evidence, identify research gaps, and establish a scientific foundation for future translational studies investigating nisin as a potential therapeutic candidate for colorectal cancer.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-11-03T18:12:05.291Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mv5zpks7mt","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mv5zpks7mt"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ade","last_name":"Sukma","orcid":"0000-0001-9940-6518"},{"first_name":"Ade","last_name":"Rakhmadi","orcid":"0009-0005-1423-7062"},{"first_name":"Irwan","last_name":"Irwan","orcid":"0000-0003-3840-234X"},{"first_name":"Fitri","last_name":"Handayani","orcid":"0000-0002-6675-5284"},{"first_name":"Nadiatul","last_name":"Aulia Zahara Rizki","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Najmiatul","last_name":"Fitria","orcid":"0000-0002-3255-1961"}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/04ded0672","name":"Andalas University","grant_id":"Research Article Review (PAR) Batch I program under Contract Number 3/UN16.19/PT.01.03/PAR/2024, funded by the Institute for Research and Community Service (Lembaga Penelitian dan Pengabdian kepada Masyarakat)"}],"categories":["Oncology","Animal","Nisin","Probiotics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"sm47g26jv4","title":"Anticancer effects of four ruthenium-cyclopentadienyl compounds in colorectal cancer cells: proteomic data","description":"Colorectal cancer (CRC) is the second most deadly type of cancer worldwide. Ruthenium compounds have emerged as promising alternatives to classical chemotherapy in the treatment of CRC. The data available here refer the proteomic study performed with the four ruthenium-cyclopentadienyl compounds in colorectal cancer cells.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-05-05T03:29:09.673Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/sm47g26jv4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/sm47g26jv4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ana Rita","last_name":"Brás","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Pedro","last_name":"Fernandes","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tiago","last_name":"Moreira","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Julia","last_name":"Morales-Sanfrutos","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Eduard","last_name":"Sabidó","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alexandra","last_name":"M.M. Antunes","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Andreia","last_name":"Valente","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ana","last_name":"Preto","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"c65rsd4fr2","title":"Extra data tables for Poulos et al \"Scarcity of recurrent regulatory driver mutations in colorectal cancer revealed by targeted deep sequencing\"","description":"Extra data tables for Poulos et al \"Scarcity of recurrent regulatory driver mutations in colorectal cancer revealed by targeted deep sequencing\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2019-04-04T14:15:11.974Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/c65rsd4fr2","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/c65rsd4fr2"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jason","last_name":"Wong","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Genomics","Colorectal Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ys6j8bndby","title":"CRC_ST","description":"Spatial transcriptomics of colorectal cancer","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-03T17:02:44.973Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ys6j8bndby","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ys6j8bndby"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Youqiong","last_name":"Ye","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["RNA Sequencing","Spatial Analysis"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":125913,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":102,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":125913,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":125415,"restricted":61,"embargoed":437},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2146},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":1329},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":597},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":450},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":421},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":394},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":389},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science 